    {
      "id":"northwoods-goal",
      "type":"goal",
      "label":"Establish what Operation Northwoods actually was",
      "position":{"x":0,"y":-350},
      "width":420,"height":220,
      "ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180}],
      "handles":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180,"portId":"root"}],
      "data":{"body":"Build a primary-source-grounded account separating documented proposals, institutional approval, presidential disposition, later claims, and speculation.","status":"in-progress","definitionKey":"goal"}
    },
    {
      "id":"northwoods-task-context",
      "type":"task",
      "label":"Place Northwoods inside the Cuba Project and Operation Mongoose",
      "position":{"x":-720,"y":50},"width":420,"height":220,
      "ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180}],
      "handles":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180,"portId":"root"}],
      "data":{"body":"Reconstruct the post-Bay of Pigs setting, Operation Mongoose, the Cuba Project, and the request that produced the March 1962 pretext memorandum.","status":"todo","definitionKey":"task"}
    },
    {
      "id":"northwoods-task-document",
      "type":"task",
      "label":"Read and map the 13 March 1962 memorandum",
      "position":{"x":-240,"y":50},"width":420,"height":220,
      "ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180}],
      "handles":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180,"portId":"root"}],
      "data":{"body":"Map authorship, recipients, stated objective, recommendations, proposed pretexts, and the distinction between preliminary planning proposals and executed operations.","status":"todo","definitionKey":"task"}
    },
    {
      "id":"northwoods-task-chain",
      "type":"task",
      "label":"Trace approval and rejection",
      "position":{"x":240,"y":50},"width":420,"height":220,
      "ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180}],
      "handles":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180,"portId":"root"}],
      "data":{"body":"Identify what the Joint Chiefs approved, what was sent to Secretary McNamara, what reached Kennedy or his advisers, and what evidence establishes that the proposals were not adopted as an operational plan.","status":"todo","definitionKey":"task"}
    },
    {
      "id":"northwoods-task-declass",
      "type":"task",
      "label":"Trace declassification and public discovery",
      "position":{"x":720,"y":50},"width":420,"height":220,
      "ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180}],
      "handles":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180,"portId":"root"}],
      "data":{"body":"Document the Assassination Records Review Board release, later publication, and how the primary document entered public historical discussion.","status":"todo","definitionKey":"task"}
    },
    {
      "id":"northwoods-question-kennedy",
      "type":"open-question",
      "label":"Exactly what did Kennedy know and reject?",
      "position":{"x":-480,"y":430},"width":420,"height":220,
      "ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180}],
      "handles":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180,"portId":"root"}],
      "data":{"body":"Distinguish documentary evidence about Kennedy's response from later summaries that may compress several Cuba-policy decisions together.","status":"open","prominence":"high","definitionKey":"open-question"}
    },
    {
      "id":"northwoods-question-execution",
      "type":"open-question",
      "label":"Were any Northwoods proposals executed?",
      "position":{"x":0,"y":430},"width":420,"height":220,
      "ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180}],
      "handles":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180,"portId":"root"}],
      "data":{"body":"Look for evidence of implementation while keeping proposals, related Mongoose covert activity, and unrelated later events analytically separate.","status":"open","prominence":"high","definitionKey":"open-question"}
    },
    {
      "id":"northwoods-question-significance",
      "type":"open-question",
      "label":"What does Northwoods demonstrate about U.S. policy-making?",
      "position":{"x":480,"y":430},"width":420,"height":220,
      "ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180}],
      "handles":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180,"portId":"root"}],
      "data":{"body":"Assess the historical significance of senior military officials formally proposing manufactured pretexts without treating the proposal itself as evidence for unrelated conspiracy claims.","status":"open","prominence":"high","definitionKey":"open-question"}
    },
    {
      "id":"northwoods-content-sources",
      "type":"content",
      "label":"Primary source anchors",
      "position":{"x":0,"y":800},"width":760,"height":300,
      "ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180}],
      "handles":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":180,"portId":"root"}],
      "data":{"markdown":"## Starting evidence\n\n- Joint Chiefs of Staff memorandum, **Justification for US Military Intervention in Cuba**, 13 March 1962.\n- Edward Lansdale, **The Cuba Project**, 20 February 1962, for Operation Mongoose context.\n- Follow-on meeting and policy records for the disposition of the proposals.\n- Declassification/publication records from the JFK Assassination Records Review Board and National Security Archive.\n\n### Research rule\nKeep three categories visibly distinct: **proposed**, **approved for further planning**, and **executed**. Northwoods is historically important precisely enough that the graph should not need exaggeration."}
    }
  ],
